  "worked_solution": "First, we find the smallest and largest $y$-values in the graph.\n\n- The smallest $y$-value is $-6.$ This occurs when $x=-2.$\n\n- The largest $y$-value is $2.$ This occurs when $x=2.$\n\nThe function covers all the $y$-values between $-6$ and $2,$ including $-6$ and $2.$\n\nTherefore, the range is $-6\\le y\\le 2,$ which can also be written as $-6\\le f(x)\\le 2.$",
